 "text": "9/29/26, 10:19 AM\n\nTriggering of the Reconnection\n\nDisconnection reason                                                                        Events that terminate the disconnection\nDisconnection dunning level reached in accounts receivable and         Clearing items, move-out\n\npayable\n\nVacant status                                                                          Move-in\n\nCustomer request                                                                    Customer request\n\nTechnical causes                                                                   Technical problems solved\n\nl\n\nYou can modify event R720 (reference check for reconnection) in the Standard function module table (which can be found in\nCustomizing for Financial Accounting (Fl)) via the program enhancement for contract accounts receivable and payable. This\nenables you to perform an amount check. You can find a reference for the program enhancement in the\nISU_CECK_RECONNETION_R720 function module (trigger reconnection upon clearing).\n\nCreate reconnection order\n\nReconnection orders are created for disconnected devices and flat-rate installations in the same way that disconnection orders are\ncreated.\n\nYou also specify whether you need to contact the corresponding customer ( Notification ) before you carry out the actual device\nreconnection.\n\nIf notification is required, the system generates a notification work item . The CRM agent assigned to this work item must contact\nthe customer, set an agreed date and close the work item before the reconnection order can be processed further\n\nIf notification is not required, or if the notification work item is closed, you can continue processing the reconnection order\n\nYou can also generate a corresponding service management (SM) service order (note however, that if notification is required, the\nsystem can only generate service orders after you have set the agreed date and the notification work item is closed).\n\nEnter reconnection and confirm reconnection order\n\nFollowing reconnection, you enter the reconnection data in the system. You can also generate a customer contact, adjust the\nbudget billing plan, post charges, and enter meter readings for the reconnection.\n\nDisconnection Document Release\n\nUse\n\nUsing the release mechanism, an agent can explicitly release disconnection documents before actual disconnection and\nreconnection processing. You cannot carry out further steps with the disconnection document (for example, generating a\ndisconnection order) until the disconnection document is released.\n\nIn this way, you can control the workload of field service employees, for example by releasing disconnection documents according\n\nSs a an i\n",
